    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d34-a7">

                <pb facs="0130" n="72" xml:id="pg72"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 7.</seg></opener>
                <head>[Translation.]</head>
                <p rendition="#center">DEPARTMENT OF STATE AND OFFICE OF WAR AND MARINE—SECTION
                    FIRST.</p>
                <p>I have informed the President of the republic of your communication of the 25th
                    of November last, dated in Cadereita Jimenez, after your evacuation of
                    Monterey.</p>
                <p>The reasons you give for that act, and your subsequent action in regard to the
                    enemy, are approved by the President, who trusts to your prudence to increase
                    and preserve the forces under your command.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left">Independence and liberty! <placeName>Paso
                            del Norte</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-01-09"
                            >January 9, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>MEJIA.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>General <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mariano Escobedo, <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Chief of the Northern Army Corps</hi>,</hi> (wherever he may
                        be.)</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
